1. Why is double more appropriate than int for the meal price and final bill?
Double is more appropriate because it can account for decimals, which most likely appear in prices, including meal prices.
2. What problem can occur if the program divides by the number of students using only integer values?
It will not show the decimal value of the prices/output
3. How does setprecision(2) improve the readability of monetary output?
It can help with the readability of the prices by giving a fixed number of decimal places.
